      "text": "To find the value(s) of \\( x \\) for which \\( f(x) = f^{-1}(x) \\), we need to follow these steps:\n\n1. **Find the inverse function \\( f^{-1}(x) \\) of \\( f(x) = 3x - 8 \\).**\n\n   To find the inverse, we start by setting \\( y = f(x) \\):\n   \\[\n   y = 3x - 8\n   \\]\n   Next, we solve for \\( x \\) in terms of \\( y \\):\n   \\[\n   y + 8 = 3x\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   x = \\frac{y + 8}{3}\n   \\]\n   Therefore, the inverse function is:\n   \\[\n   f^{-1}(x) = \\frac{x + 8}{3}\n   \\]\n\n2. **Set \\( f(x) \\) equal to \\( f^{-1}(x) \\) and solve for \\( x \\).**\n\n   We need to find \\( x \\) such that:\n   \\[\n   f(x) = f^{-1}(x)\n   \\]\n   Substitute \\( f(x) = 3x - 8 \\) and \\( f^{-1}(x) = \\frac{x + 8}{3} \\) into the equation:\n   \\[\n   3x - 8 = \\frac{x + 8}{3}\n   \\]\n   To eliminate the fraction, multiply both sides by 3:\n   \\[\n   3(3x - 8) = x + 8\n   \\]\n   Simplify the left side:\n   \\[\n   9x - 24 = x + 8\n   \\]\n   Rearrange the equation to isolate \\( x \\):\n   \\[\n   9x - x = 8 + 24\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   8x = 32\n   \\]\n   Solve for \\( x \\):\n   \\[\n   x = \\frac{32}{8}\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   x = 4\n   \\]\n\n3. **Verify the solution.**\n\n   Substitute \\( x = 4 \\) back into the original function \\( f(x) \\):\n   \\[\n   f(4) = 3(4) - 8 = 12 - 8 = 4\n   \\]\n   Now, substitute \\( x = 4 \\) into the inverse function \\( f^{-1}(x) \\):\n   \\[\n   f^{-1}(4) = \\frac{4 + 8}{3} = \\frac{12}{3} = 4\n   \\]\n   Since \\( f(4) = 4 \\) and \\( f^{-1}(4) = 4 \\), the solution is verified.\n\nTherefore, the value of \\( x \\) for which \\( f(x) = f^{-1}(x) \\) is \\(\\boxed{4}\\).",
