      "text": "Given the function \\( f(x) = 3x - 8 \\), we need to find the inverse function \\( f^{-1}(x) \\). To do this, we start by setting \\( y = f(x) \\), so we have:\n\n\\[ y = 3x - 8 \\]\n\nNext, we solve for \\( x \\) in terms of \\( y \\):\n\n\\[ y + 8 = 3x \\]\n\\[ x = \\frac{y + 8}{3} \\]\n\nThus, the inverse function is:\n\n\\[ f^{-1}(x) = \\frac{x + 8}{3} \\]\n\nWe need to find the value of \\( x \\) for which \\( f(x) = f^{-1}(x) \\). Therefore, we set up the equation:\n\n\\[ f(x) = f^{-1}(x) \\]\n\\[ 3x - 8 = \\frac{x + 8}{3} \\]\n\nTo eliminate the fraction, we multiply both sides of the equation by 3:\n\n\\[ 3(3x - 8) = x + 8 \\]\n\\[ 9x - 24 = x + 8 \\]\n\nNext, we isolate \\( x \\) by subtracting \\( x \\) from both sides:\n\n\\[ 9x - x - 24 = 8 \\]\n\\[ 8x - 24 = 8 \\]\n\nThen, we add 24 to both sides:\n\n\\[ 8x = 32 \\]\n\nFinally, we divide both sides by 8:\n\n\\[ x = 4 \\]\n\nTo verify, we substitute \\( x = 4 \\) back into the original functions \\( f(x) \\) and \\( f^{-1}(x) \\):\n\n\\[ f(4) = 3(4) - 8 = 12 - 8 = 4 \\]\n\\[ f^{-1}(4) = \\frac{4 + 8}{3} = \\frac{12}{3} = 4 \\]\n\nSince \\( f(4) = f^{-1}(4) = 4 \\), our solution is correct. Therefore, the value of \\( x \\) for which \\( f(x) = f^{-1}(x) \\) is:\n\n\\[ \\boxed{4} \\]",
