      "sample_index": 3,
      "text": "Given $f(x)=3x-8$, we first find the inverse function $f^{-1}(x)$.\n\nTo find the inverse, set $y=f(x)$ and solve for $x$ in terms of $y$:\n\n\\[y = 3x - 8\\]\n\n\\[y + 8 = 3x\\]\n\n\\[x = \\frac{y + 8}{3}\\]\n\nThus, the inverse function is:\n\n\\[f^{-1}(x) = \\frac{x + 8}{3}\\]\n\nWe want to find the value(s) of $x$ such that $f(x) = f^{-1}(x)$. Set $f(x)$ equal to $f^{-1}(x)$ and solve for $x$:\n\n\\[3x - 8 = \\frac{x + 8}{3}\\]\n\nMultiply both sides by $3$ to clear the fraction:\n\n\\[3(3x - 8) = x + 8\\]\n\n\\[9x - 24 = x + 8\\]\n\nSubtract $x$ from both sides:\n\n\\[8x - 24 = 8\\]\n\nAdd $24$ to both sides:\n\n\\[8x = 32\\]\n\nDivide by $8$:\n\n\\[x = 4\\]\n\nTherefore, the value of $x$ for which $f(x) = f^{-1}(x)$ is $\\boxed{4}$.",
